# Pre-deadline review

When the user asks to run the pre-deadline / GW / news review (including from the Cursor phone app):

## 1. Show the saved squad, then confirm

Do **not** run `predeadline` yet.

Load the last snapshot: use `data/private-state/current.json` if present, otherwise `uv run fpl-agent team-state materialize-from-env` (never print the secret or raw JSON).

List it in **names**, not ID dumps: 15 players, captain, vice, bank in £m, free transfers, and when it was last saved. Map IDs via public FPL `web_name`.

Then ask, and **wait**:

> Is this still your team? If anything changed (transfers, captain, bank, FT), send an FPL app screenshot of the picks/pitch. If nothing changed, say **unchanged**.

- Photo already attached on this message → skip the question; go to step 2.
- They say **unchanged** → set `as_of` to now (UTC) so the file is fresh, validate, then step 3. No photo required.
- They say something changed, or the list is missing/unreadable → **wait for a photo**. Do not guess.
- No saved squad at all → ask for a photo immediately.

If bank, FT, or chips are not on the first screenshot, ask for a second (transfers / team page). If a name is ambiguous, ask. Never invent player IDs.

## 2. Update the squad file from the photo (only if they sent one)

Write `data/private-state/current.json` (gitignored):

- Set `as_of` to now (UTC) and `applies_before_gameweek` to the next GW.
- Map visible names to official FPL `id` values (bootstrap `web_name` / full name).
- Keep previous `purchase_prices_tenths` for players still in the 15. For new players, use listed `now_cost` if the buy price is not on the photo, and say so.
- Update bank (`bank_tenths`: £1.5m → `15`), `free_transfers`, `captain_id`, `vice_id`, starters/bench if visible.
- Confirm in words: 15 names, bank, FT, captain. Do not paste the full JSON.

Then: `uv run fpl-agent team-state validate data/private-state/current.json`

If `gh` is available, also `uv run fpl-agent team-state encode-for-github data/private-state/current.json` so the evening GitHub job matches.

## 3. Run the review

`uv run fpl-agent predeadline --live-ai`  
Add `--force` only if they ask, or if the gate says it is too early/late and they still want it.

Show the CLI report. Do not invent transfers, prices, player IDs, or news.

Cursor's model picker may stay Auto. OpenAI for news is `OPENAI_API_KEY` inside `predeadline`. The user makes all FPL changes themselves.

The CLI writes `reports/predeadline-gw*.md` and refreshes the latest-results block in `README.md`.

Price watch is GitHub Actions (`fpl-agent prices`). Do not start that job from chat unless asked.

## 4. Push to GitHub and merge (required after every successful review)

The phone README links only work on the **default branch** (`main`). A local commit, an open feature-branch PR, or a draft PR is **not** done — you will not see it on GitHub until it is on `main`.

After the CLI saves a new `reports/predeadline-gw*.md` and updates `README.md`, publish immediately — even if the user did not say commit, push, or merge:

1. Stage **only** `README.md` and the new `reports/predeadline-gw*.md` file (plus this rule / README publish wording if you had to edit those).
2. Commit, for example: `Pre-deadline GW{N} review`.
3. Push the working branch: `git push -u origin HEAD`.
4. Open or update the PR targeting `main` if the Cloud Agent flow created one.
5. **Merge that PR into `main` in the same run.** Do not leave it open. If a GitHub merge API is unavailable, fast-forward `main` locally and `git push origin main` so the PR closes as merged. Mark a draft PR ready first if merge is blocked by draft status.
6. Do not finish the run until `origin/main` has the new report and README link. Retry on network errors.

Never stage: `.env`, `data/private-state/**`, JSON reports, price snapshots, caches, or unrelated code. Private squad state stays gitignored.
